# Cloudflare Turnstile protects the three contact forms.
# Create a widget for the production domain in the Cloudflare dashboard
# (Turnstile, Add widget), then copy its two keys into the hosting settings.
# In production, when one of them is missing the forms refuse every request.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is read at build time: redeploy after setting it.
#
# The values below are Cloudflare's public TEST keys (the widget always passes).
# They are only for local work: on any Vercel deployment the forms refuse them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
